# ── Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# config_base/config.json is the authoritative one; sync_config.py copies it
# down to IAF_AI/config.json. Both hold real provider keys once you fill them
# in, so neither is tracked. Copy the example and edit that:
#     cp config_base/config.example.json config_base/config.json
config_base/config.json
IAF_AI/config.json

# ── Runtime state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The conversation record, the per-turn session directories, and whatever the
# engine writes while running. Directories are kept via .gitkeep.
workspace/*
!workspace/.gitkeep
pool/threads/*
!pool/threads/.gitkeep
pool/semantic.md
IAF_AI/dispatch/*/sessions/*
!IAF_AI/dispatch/*/sessions/.gitkeep
IAF_AI/dispatch/speaker/memory/*
!IAF_AI/dispatch/speaker/memory/.gitkeep
IAF_AI/dispatch/speaker/staging/*
!IAF_AI/dispatch/speaker/staging/.gitkeep

# ── Recordings ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Session dumps and any corpus you record. Never commit recordings of a real
# person's speech. README.md explains how to record and label your own.
IAF_AI/dispatch/listener/fixtures/*
!IAF_AI/dispatch/listener/fixtures/.gitkeep
!IAF_AI/dispatch/listener/fixtures/README.md
IAF_AI/dispatch/voice_out/fixtures/*
!IAF_AI/dispatch/voice_out/fixtures/.gitkeep
!IAF_AI/dispatch/voice_out/fixtures/README.md

# ── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# ── OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
